The sixth item is the open twin of the closed item \emph{why they cannot
see it}: a commit made an hour ago, a teammate's fresh clone of the
shared repository that does not contain it, and two questions---what has
happened, and what the student would do.
An account that says the commit is on the student's own computer until
it is sent has discerned the local/remote distinction of
\cref{sec:remotes} unprompted; an account that blames the teammate's
clone, or has the commit \enquote{still uploading}, has not.
The stem does not say that nothing was pushed: that sentence would name
the missing step, which is what the student is to supply
\autocite[p.~91]{NCOL}; the closed twin leaves it out for the same
reason.

