History is a graph of commits linked to their parents, not a folder of
versions (\cref{sec:model}).
The item shows a three-line history and asks where the first version is
kept and how it comes back.
The correct answer names a commit in the repository, linked to the one
after it, from which Git can restore the project as it was; the leading
distractor is the folder-of-versions picture---one sub-folder per saved
version, opened in the file manager---the file-storage model documented
from repository data \autocite{Cochez2013DVCSUsage}; the others keep only
the latest version, or a single backup file.

