\subsubsection{The staging area}

[[git add]] stages an existing change for the next commit, moving it
from the working tree into the index (\cref{sec:staging}).
The item shows the command on a file that already exists and was just
edited, and asks what it does.
Two distractors are documented misconceptions: that [[git add file]]
creates a file rather than staging it \autocite[Sec.~5.3]{IsomottonenCochez2014},
and the add-as-commit reading that it already records the version; the
last has it upload the file to the shared repository.

