The end quiz shows, with the correct alternative, this account of why:

<<feedback: what git add does>>=
"feedback": {"neutral": "<p>git add marks an existing change to be included in the next commit&mdash;it moves the change into the staging area, the set of changes the next commit will record. It does not create the file, it records nothing in the history yet (that is git commit), and it sends nothing anywhere (that is git push).</p>"}
