The end quiz shows, with the correct alternative, this account of why:

<<feedback: what status shows after an edit>>=
"feedback": {"neutral": "<p>git status compares three things: the files as they are on disk, what is staged for the next commit, and the last commit. A saved edit differs from the last commit and is not yet staged, so the file is listed under &ldquo;Changes not staged for commit&rdquo;. Saving alone stages nothing, and status reads every file without an add first.</p>"}
