\subsubsection{Branches}

A branch is a movable pointer into the commit graph, not a place you
move into (\cref{sec:branches}).
The item names a branch and asks how to see the files as they are on
it.
The key distractor is the branch-as-directory misconception---trying to
[[cd]] into a branch---the best-documented Git misconception in the
literature \autocite[Sec.~5.2]{IsomottonenCochez2014}; the others look
for the branch as a folder inside [[.git]] or copy it in.
The correct answer switches, and the files in the same folder change to
those of the branch: that the files on disk depend on the current
branch is exactly the hidden dependency named by
\textcite{Church2014HiddenDependencies}.
The open twin \emph{the branch called feature} (\cref{app:open-items})
asks the same situation without alternatives.

