\subsubsection{Remotes and collaboration}

Every clone is complete: it holds the whole history, and there is no
\enquote{main} copy by mechanism, only by convention
(\cref{sec:remotes}).
The item puts the student offline with yesterday's clone and asks what
[[git log]] shows.
The correct answer is the whole history as it was at the clone; the
distractors keep the history on GitHub and need a connection, fetch
earlier commits on demand, or show only the student's own commits.
This item opens the remote items because it stands on its own;
the two that follow compare the local and the shared copy, which this
one has just established to be two full copies.

